[CENTER][SIZE=6][B][COLOR=#FF5A36]SOS-Staff[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
[SIZE=3]Free, open-source support-ticket management with a full bidirectional Discord bridge.[/SIZE][/CENTER]

[hr]

[SIZE=4][B]What it does[/B][/SIZE]
Players open tickets in-game. Staff manage them from Discord. Live chat relays both ways for as long as the ticket stays open - no server-hopping between Minecraft and Discord to get help.

[SIZE=4][B]Features[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B]Two creation flows[/B] - a preset list of common issues, free-form text (anvil GUI or chat), or both, configurable globally and per category.
[*][B]Anti-spam[/B] - a configurable cap on open tickets per player and a cooldown after closing one.
[*][B]Bidirectional live chat[/B] - a player's in-game messages relay instantly to their ticket's Discord channel via webhook (their own skin and name), and staff replies relay back in-game.
[*][B]One Discord channel per ticket[/B], with claim/close/reopen/priority/transcript/ping buttons and fully configurable, permission-gated action buttons (heal, feed, force-reconnect, teleport, freeze, or any raw command).
[*][B]In-game admin panel[/B] ([I]/sostaff panel[/I]) - a paginated, filterable ticket list with player heads, status-colored wool, and click-to-teleport-and-attach-chat.
[*][B]Five shipped languages[/B] at parity: English, French, Spanish, Russian, German.
[*][B]Hot reload[/B] ([I]/sostaff reload[/I]) - config, language files, and the Discord connection, without ever disrupting a ticket already open.
[*][B]GDPR tooling[/B] - [I]/sostaff gdpr erase <player>[/I] and configurable transcript retention.
[*][B]A public API and Bukkit events[/B] for other plugins to read, create, and react to tickets.
[*][B]Soft-depend integrations[/B] - PlaceholderAPI, LuckPerms, Vault.
[*][B]Folia-safe[/B] throughout.
[/LIST]

[SIZE=4][B]Requirements[/B][/SIZE]
Paper (or a fork such as Purpur/DivineMC) [B]26.2 or newer[/B] - which itself requires [B]Java 25[/B]. A Discord bot application of your own (free, five minutes to set up - see the wiki linked below).

[hr]

